HAProxy patches
===============

This directory holds the patches that must be applied to a stock HAProxy source
tree before the OTel filter can be built into it.  Every subdirectory carries
the series for one HAProxy branch, applied in order.

These patches are not officially supported.  They are meant only for users who
still need the filter on an older HAProxy branch.

Layout:

  3.2/  series for the HAProxy 3.2 branch
  3.3/  series for the HAProxy 3.3 branch

Each file is a mailbox patch produced by git format-patch.  The From and index
lines in its header name a commit and blobs of the tree the patch was made in,
not the HAProxy tar file it is made for, so these hashes mean nothing here and
a three way merge against them is not possible.  Apply a series with the patch
tool from the directory where the tar was unpacked, in order:

  % cd haproxy-3.2.*
  % patch -p1 < /path/to/patches/3.2/0*.patch

On a HAProxy git checkout the same files can go in as commits, since they are
git format patches:

  % git am /path/to/patches/3.2/0*.patch

Take the series that matches the branch you build; both patches of a series are
required, the addon will not build without them.

  0001-BUILD-add-an-EXTRA_MAKE-option-to-build-addons-easil.patch
      Adds the EXTRA_MAKE make variable.  The top level Makefile includes the
      Makefile.mk fragment of every directory listed there, which is how the
      OTel addon, living outside the HAProxy tree, is plugged into the build.

  0002-MINOR-otel-added-ARGC_OTEL-enum.patch
      Adds the ARGC_OTEL argument context to arg-t.h and sample.c.  The addon
      sets it on the otel-scope arguments, so without this patch the filter
      fails to compile; it also names the otel-scope directive in the error
      message when a fetch keyword inside it fails.
